From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 07:17:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Optionally boost the submit path
 while work is in flight

A light render or compute stream keeps 64 submissions in flight, yet a
command finds fewer than two others queued at the firmware when it
starts: the work between the scheduler and the firmware arrives late.
That work runs on drm_sched's ordered, normal-priority workqueue and
on whatever CPU and clock the governor gives short kernel work, which
on the J604 is often an efficiency core near 0.9 GHz.

Add g16_submit_boost (runtime, default 0). Bit 0: queues created from
then on run their scheduler work on a high-priority ordered reclaim
workqueue (new OwnedQueue::new_ordered_reclaim_highpri). Bit 1: every
cpufreq policy gets a minimum-frequency request at its top frequency
from the first command in flight until the busy period ends (the same
window as g16_lat_qos_us, also dropped at fail-stop), so idle power
does not change. A performance-core cpumask is not set: an ordered
workqueue's attributes cannot be changed, and a module cannot apply
workqueue attributes.

Assisted-by: LLM
